usage: app [-h] [-c COUNT] [-v] [--dry-run] [--name NAME] --ratio R
           [--tag TAG] [--out OUT]
           [--a-very-long-option-name-here A_VERY_LONG_OPTION_NAME_HERE]
           files [files ...] {fast,slow}

Process some files and do a number of interesting things with them, wrapping
onto a second line.

positional arguments:
  files                 input files
  {fast,slow}           how to run

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -c COUNT, --count COUNT
                        how many times (default: 1)
  -v, --verbose
  --dry-run             don't change anything
  --name NAME           a name
  --ratio R
  --tag TAG             tags, can repeat
  --out OUT
  --a-very-long-option-name-here A_VERY_LONG_OPTION_NAME_HERE
                        this help text is long enough that it will need to
                        wrap around onto the following line of output

See the docs for more.
---
